#![enable(implicit_some)]
// What each profession is: what it asks of a character, what it gives, what
// it can do. One row for each, named as `Profession` names it. A row lists
// only what is not the default (empty, none, false, 0).
//
//   minimums              the attribute scores it asks for (none: no minimum)
//                         (retail `g_profession_table`)
//   hit_points            hit points a level gives, before the vitality
//                         factor `0.6 + 0.008 * VIT` (`g_profession_table`)
//   experience            the experience its first level costs; later levels
//                         double to level 10, then grow by a fifth
//   bonus_skill           the skill it trains best: a quarter more than the
//                         points put in, at least one
//   skills                the other skills a new member of it starts with
//   physical              how heavily its levels weigh in a hand's physical
//                         score
//   open_skills           the ordinary and book skills it may train
//                         (`g_profession_skill_availability`); the realm
//                         skills follow the spells learned, the expert skills
//                         the attributes
//   traits                what it can do besides (retail trait description
//                         order)
//   books                 the spellbooks it casts from
//                         (`g_profession_spellbooks`)
//   caster_offset         added to its levels to give its caster level: 0 for
//                         the pure casters, -4 for the hybrids, who cast from
//                         their fifth level; left out, it cannot cast
//                         (`g_profession_magic_level_offsets`)
//   picks_from_any_book   the spells it is awarded may be from any book,
//                         not only its first
//   only_gender           the only gender it may be
//   resistance            added to every realm's resistance
//   starting_items        the items a new member of it carries, by retail
//                         item number (`g_starting_equipment`); a race may
//                         have its own set instead
//   extra_item            and one more (`AddCharacterStartingEquipment`):
//                         Always(item), or ByTrainedSkill: `then` if the
//                         member trains `skill` further than `over`,
//                         otherwise `otherwise`
{
    Fighter: (
        minimums: {Strength: 55, Vitality: 50, Dexterity: 50},
        hit_points: 9.0,
        experience: 1000,
